AB  - This paper introduces GenASPEN, a collaborative AI agentic ecosystem for automatic performance modeling and prediction. To our knowledge, GenASPEN is the first system to integrate generative AI, analytical modeling, and human expertise in a unified agentic workflow for automatic performance modeling of high performance computing (HPC) applications. It includes a code translation agent that leverages both a finetuned model and a context-aware chain-of-thought reasoning pipeline to convert HPC code into abstract application models, as well as a performance modeling agent that invokes tools that combine application and machine models to generate predictions. Evaluations of a range of essential HPC and AI workloads, benchmarks and applications-including BLAS routines, a conjugate gradient solver, XSBench, LULESH, and MiniMDock-show that GenASPEN predicts key operations (e.g., floating-point operations, loads, and stores) with 98% accuracy, which contributes to highly accurate predictions of execution time (average accuracies of 94.40% and 93.09%) for modern NVIDIA and AMD GPUs. Compared with current frontier LLMs that use trillions or hundreds of billions of parameters (e.g., ChatGPT-5.5, Claude-Opus-4.7, Gemini-3.1), GenASPEN's hybrid approach with 7, 20, and 120 billion parameter models and modest hardware resources achieves superior GPU execution time prediction accuracy in 73% of cases and competitive accuracy in the other instances.
ER  - 

