AB  - The rapid evolution of software development demands innovative approaches to enhance security, efficiency, and automation throughout the Software Development Lifecycle (SDLC). This paper presents a comprehensive Generative AI-assisted framework that integrates large language models and machine learning techniques to optimize and secure the SDLC. The proposed framework leverages generative AI capabilities across multiple phases including requirements analysis, code generation, vulnerability detection, automated testing, and deployment optimization. By incorporating AI-driven threat modeling and continuous security assessment, the framework addresses critical challenges in identifying vulnerabilities early in development while maintaining code quality and reducing time-to-market. The system employs advanced prompt engineering techniques and context-aware code analysis to generate secure code patterns, detect security anomalies, and suggest remediation strategies in real-time. Experimental validation demonstrates significant improvements in vulnerability detection rates, code quality metrics, and development efficiency compared to traditional SDLC approaches. The framework achieves automated security scanning with minimal false positives while maintaining developer productivity. This research contributes to the emerging field of AI-assisted software engineering by providing a practical, scalable solution for organizations seeking to modernize their development processes while prioritizing security and autonomy.
ER  - 

